    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d39">

                <pb facs="0136" n="16" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg16"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Brown to the
                            Acting Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation to Guatemala and Honduras</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1905-07-05"><hi rendition="#italic">July 5,
                                1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 288.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith
                    copies with translations appended of the expressions of condolence on the death
                    of Mr. Hay received by this legation from the Governments of Guatemala and
                    Honduras.</p>
                <p>The spontaneous expression of sympathy from President Estrada Cabrera seems to me
                    to be marked by a sincere appreciation of the dead statesman and a true spirit
                    of friendship toward the United States.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Philip Brown.</hi></signed></closer>





